      "text": "To find the value of \\(0.\\overline{789} - 0.\\overline{456} - 0.\\overline{123}\\), we first need to convert each repeating decimal into a fraction.\n\n1. Convert \\(0.\\overline{789}\\) to a fraction:\n    Let \\(x = 0.\\overline{789}\\).\n    Then, \\(1000x = 789.\\overline{789}\\).\n    So, \\(1000x - x = 789.\\overline{789} - 0.\\overline{789}\\), which gives \\(999x = 789\\).\n    Therefore, \\(x = \\frac{789}{999}\\).\n\n2. Convert \\(0.\\overline{456}\\) to a fraction:\n    Let \\(y = 0.\\overline{456}\\).\n    Then, \\(1000y = 456.\\overline{456}\\).\n    So, \\(1000y - y = 456.\\overline{456} - 0.\\overline{456}\\), which gives \\(999y = 456\\).\n    Therefore, \\(y = \\frac{456}{999}\\).\n\n3. Convert \\(0.\\overline{123}\\) to a fraction:\n    Let \\(z = 0.\\overline{123}\\).\n    Then, \\(1000z = 123.\\overline{123}\\).\n    So, \\(1000z - z = 123.\\overline{123} - 0.\\overline{123}\\), which gives \\(999z = 123\\).\n    Therefore, \\(z = \\frac{123}{999}\\).\n\nNow we need to find the value of \\(0.\\overline{789} - 0.\\overline{456} - 0.\\overline{123}\\):\n\\[\n0.\\overline{789} - 0.\\overline{456} - 0.\\overline{123} = \\frac{789}{999} - \\frac{456}{999} - \\frac{123}{999}.\n\\]\nSince the denominators are the same, we can combine the numerators:\n\\[\n\\frac{789 - 456 - 123}{999} = \\frac{789 - 579}{999} = \\frac{210}{999}.\n\\]\nNow we need to simplify the fraction \\(\\frac{210}{999}\\). We find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 210 and 999, which is 3, so we divide both the numerator and the denominator by 3:\n\\[\n\\frac{210 \\div 3}{999 \\div 3} = \\frac{70}{333}.\n\\]\nTherefore, the value of \\(0.\\overline{789} - 0.\\overline{456} - 0.\\overline{123}\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{70}{333}}\\).",
