      "text": "Let $x=0.\\overline{789}$. We can write this as $1000x=789.\\overline{789}$. Subtracting the two equations, we get $999x=789$, so $x=\\boxed{\\frac{789}{999}}$.\n\nFor $0.\\overline{456}$, let $y=0.\\overline{456}$. We can write this as $1000y=456.\\overline{456}$. Subtracting the two equations, we get $999y=456$, so $y=\\boxed{\\frac{456}{999}}$.\n\nSimilarly, for $0.\\overline{123}$, let $z=0.\\overline{123}$. We can write this as $1000z=123.\\overline{123}$. Subtracting the two equations, we get $999z=123$, so $z=\\boxed{\\frac{123}{999}}$.\n\nTo find the value of $x-y-z$, we subtract the fractions: \\[\nx-y-z = \\frac{789}{999} - \\frac{456}{999} - \\frac{123}{999} = \\boxed{\\frac{210}{999}}. \n\\] The answer is: \\frac{210}{999}",
